<exercise><exercise data-wait-for-event="RFM1">
  <div class="os-raise-ib-input-ack">
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Typically, we define repeated exponents by working down the tower, e.g., \(2^{3^5}=2^{\left(3^5\right)}\). One reason for this is that evaluating up the tower, as in \(\left(2^3\right)^5\), can already be simplified by using algebra rules (in this case, to get \(2^{15}\)).</para>
  </div>
<problem>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
      <br/>
      <item> Which of the two would you choose as the meaning of the expression \(2^{3^5}\) written without parentheses? </item>
    </list>
  </problem><solution>
